 "text": "Monopoly was invented to show how unfair monopolies are. 1904. Lizzie Magie patents a board game called The Landlord's Game. Players buy property, charge rent, and watch others go broke. She wanted people to see how unfair that is. For years, people make their own homemade copies. Players in Atlantic City add their own street names. Then, in the 1930s, a man named Charles Darrow sells a version to Parker Brothers. He's credited as the inventor. Royalties make him a millionaire. Lizzie? Parker Brothers buys her patent for $500. The truth only comes out in the 1970s during a court fight over another board game. A game about unfairness with an unfair origin story. Every legend has a beginning.",
